+PR CI builds and tests native candidates on Linux x64, Windows x64 and Apple Silicon, plus the container, extension and contract checks. macOS Intel runs after merge on main. When the main tree is identical to the merged PR's tested merge ref, main promotes that PR run's three native candidates and builds only Intel. A main push that changes dependency, toolchain, Docker, nextest or CI inputs, or that cannot authenticate the PR producer, rebuilds all four targets. Native builds and runtime validation use separate jobs with a verified same-run payload handoff. Routine managed MCP validation runs one full pass plus two extra cold-client regression passes while the Intel failure remains unresolved; qualification runs three full passes. Failed passes are not retried. Rerun all CI jobs for a complete release attempt: successful build jobs can reuse their exact earlier payload and passed regression evidence in that run; `fresh_build` disables reuse. See [native build reuse](docs/ci-and-builds.md#native-build-reuse-and-darwin-failure-diagnostics).
 
-Hosted runners have four logical processors, so deadline races that hosted CI exposes may not appear on a high-core workstation. Before a PR that touches native service, MCP, installer or smoke-test code, run `pwsh -File scripts/ci-local.ps1` on Windows. It builds a fresh release pair, then repeats the managed MCP, native-client and installed-process smokes five times while every child process is restricted to four processors. `-Cores`, `-Repeat`, `-Load` and `-Suites` adjust it; `-SkipBuild` reuses `artifacts/runtime/x86_64-pc-windows-msvc`; add `-RuntimeDir <path>` to select a separately staged pair without replacing that default. Its logs stay in ignored `artifacts/ci-local/`. Native test reads must use the shared typed-retry helpers in `packages/vscode/src/test/nativeReadRetry.ts`. A raw MCP call that must run exactly once, such as a deliberate negative test, needs a `// native read:` comment that gives the reason. Every native error assertion includes the reply. `scripts/tests/test_native_read_contract.py` enforces these rules.
